1.0.4 2026-11-02

  - derivatives/stimulus_events: the second row of each duplicated trigger (1-50 us apart, same sample, sequence and
    code) dropped: 156,902 rows; summary columns added; code/fix-20261030_dedup_stimulus_events.py.
  - sub-P013 channels.tsv (3 runs): EMG1/EMG2 typed EMG (were MISC; header labels); ieeg.json channel counts.
  - So that no published row is lost, the 111 events.tsv files of version 1.0.2 are kept byte for byte at the same
    relative paths under sourcedata/events-v1.0.2/ (with a README). 501,835 published rows = 251,433 in
    derivatives/stimulus_events + 5 in sourcedata/events-removed-2026-10-17 + 93,495 exact duplicates + 156,902
    second rows of duplicated triggers.
  - README: the published text is kept unchanged; sections "Duplicated triggers and EMG channels" and "Published
    events.tsv files kept in sourcedata" added after it.
  - Version 1.0.4 also contains the 1.0.3 changes below, which were never released on their own.

1.0.3 2026-10-17
  - events.tsv: removed 5 Letswave sequence-name events of sub-P013 (3 files) whose onsets lay after the end of the recording; removed rows kept in sourcedata/events-removed-2026-10-17/. Signal files unchanged.
  - README.md: section "Events outside the data".
  - events.tsv of the 111 epoched files: exactly one row per epoch (331 epochs; count from the data headers), so mne_bids.read_epochs_bids loads each file as its epochs (before: Event time samples were not unique; No matching events found). The other 408335 rows of 111 files moved unchanged to derivatives/stimulus_events/ (same paths; dataset_description.json, README.md, events JSON, per-file summary); 93495 rows identical to an earlier row dropped. Code: code/fix-20261018_split_stimulus_events.py.
  - README: section 'Events and epochs (18 Oct 2026)'.

